Subject: [PATCH] apt, ptm, qt: Close 3DS Lid

Emulation > Close 3DS Lid (hotkey Ctrl+D, checkable) closes and opens the
emulated 3DS lid. Some games only do something while the 3DS is closed:
nintendogs + cats counts its walk while the lid is shut and never asks for
steps while it is open.

Closing sets PTM's shell state (GetShellState) and sends SleepQuery to the
running software. When it accepts (ReplySleepQuery, until now a stub) it
gets SleepAccepted. Opening sends SleepAwake, or SleepCancelledByOpen when
the sleep wasn't accepted yet. The request from the frontend is applied on
the emulation thread (the APT button update event). Emulation keeps
running meanwhile, so the clock and the virtual pedometer (Steps per hour)
go on as on a sleeping 3DS. A new game starts with the lid open.

